---
import Guide from '../../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Checkpoint from '../../../components/Checkpoint.astro';
import Lines from '../../../components/guide/Lines.astro';
import { CHECKPOINTS, EXAMPLE_GRADE, SCENARIO } from '../../../data/bug-walkthrough';
import { fill } from '../../../data/swe-prose';
import swe from '../../../data/swe.json';
import { url } from '../../../lib/url';

const planLine = fill('format-plan', [
  'SettingsForm.tsx, SettingsForm.test.tsx',
  'persist the preference before reporting success',
  'save, recreate the page, and read the saved value',
]);
const intentLine = fill('format-intent', [
  'update memory without saving the preference',
  'the saved preference to survive refresh',
  'saved settings survive refresh',
]);
---

<Guide title="Bug walkthrough" description="Follow an illustrative settings bug from reproduction to handoff: the conditions, evidence, and return paths of an agent following SWE.">
  <section aria-labelledby="top">
    <p class="eyebrow">One bug · a guarded path</p>
    <h1 id="top">What makes a fix ready?</h1>
    <p class="lead">“{SCENARIO}”</p>
    <p>
      Follow an agent using SWE from that report to a reviewable change. Each checkpoint explains
      what must be true before the work advances—and what happens when it is not.
    </p>
    <aside class="example-note" aria-label="About this example">
      <strong>Illustrative example, not a captured run.</strong>
      The app, filenames, grade, and evidence below are made up. The method and format shapes
      are linked to the pinned rulebook. No commands or tests were executed for this story.
    </aside>
    <nav class="story-path" aria-label="Walkthrough stages">
      <ol>{CHECKPOINTS.map((checkpoint) => <li><a href={`#${checkpoint.id}`}>{checkpoint.stage}</a></li>)}</ol>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="responsibility">
    <h2 id="responsibility">The agent does the work. SWE sets the method.</h2>
    <p>
      These checkpoints are <strong>Agent instructions</strong>. They do not imply that a script
      can decide whether this bug is fixed. A <strong>Hook check</strong> can block or warn about a
      specific supported action when installed; it does not certify the whole result.
      <strong> Your decision</strong> is needed when intent is unclear, approval is required, or the change is ready for review.
    </p>
    <p class="small">
      “Held” and “Condition satisfied” describe this story’s progress. They are editorial labels,
      not literal Kerby output. <a href={url('rulebooks/swe/hooks/')}>See what hooks actually check.</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  {CHECKPOINTS.map((checkpoint, index) => (
    <Checkpoint checkpoint={checkpoint} index={index}>
      {checkpoint.id === 'explain' && <>
        <figure class="code-example">
          <figcaption>Illustrative filename: SettingsForm.tsx · the missing persistence step</figcaption>
          <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Illustrative persistence code"><code>{`function save(nextPreference) {\n  setPreference(nextPreference); // memory only\n  setMessage('Saved');\n}\n\n// On a fresh page, the unchanged stored value wins.\nconst initialPreference = preferencesStore.read();`}</code></pre>
        </figure>
        <Lines kind="example" lines={[intentLine]} caption="An illustrative intent statement using SWE’s source-derived format." />
      </>}
      {checkpoint.id === 'plan' && <>
        <Lines kind="example" lines={[planLine]} caption="An illustrative plan line; these filenames are not part of Kerby." />
        <p class="small">
          Grade {EXAMPLE_GRADE} is an example judgment for a focused change using an existing store.
          The default full-plan threshold is {swe.numbers.planThreshold}; the grade-based approval stop is
          {' '}{swe.numbers.approvalGrade}. This example does not introduce a mandatory approval pause.
          <a href={url('rulebooks/swe/workflows/#grade')}> Read how scope and risk change the route.</a>
        </p>
      </>}
      {checkpoint.id === 'fix' && <div class="test-pair" aria-label="Illustrative regression check before and after the fix">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Before the fix</p><h3>Failure captured</h3><p>The test saves “off,” recreates the page, and observes “on.” It catches the original problem.</p></div>
        <div><p class="eyebrow">After the fix</p><h3>Condition satisfied</h3><p>The same test observes “off.” Continue to broader checks and the actual refresh behavior.</p></div>
      </div>}
      {checkpoint.id === 'verify' && <aside class="return-path" aria-labelledby="held-heading">
        <span class="return-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↶</span>
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Held · example failure branch</p><h3 id="held-heading">Not ready to call this fixed.</h3>
          <p>If the setting still disappears after refresh, preserve that failed observation. Investigate the persistence path again; do not treat a passing isolated check as completion.</p>
          <a href="#explain">Return to Explain: investigate the cause</a>
        </div>
      </aside>}
    </Checkpoint>
  ))}

  <section aria-labelledby="handoff">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your decision</p>
    <h2 id="handoff">Ready for review is a visible handoff.</h2>
    <p>
      In real work, the agent includes fresh verification results and manual instructions, records the
      required project state, and leaves the committed change ready for review. You can examine both
      the change and its evidence before deciding what happens next. This story has no real commit,
      test run, or shipped fix behind it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`https://github.com/${swe.source_repo}/blob/${swe.source_sha}/skills/kerby/rulebooks/swe/workflows/bugfix.md#6-finish`}>Read the source workflow’s finish requirements</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="next-h">
    <h2 id="next-h">Read next</h2>
    <ul class="next">
      <li><a href={url('rulebooks/swe/workflows/')}><strong>Workflows</strong><span>How other tasks change the route and planning.</span></a></li>
      <li><a href={url('rulebooks/swe/hooks/')}><strong>Hooks</strong><span>The actions a supported hook can check.</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Guide>

<style>
  .example-note { border-left: 2px solid var(--structure); padding: .8rem 1.2rem; margin: 1.8rem 0; color: var(--secondary); }
  .example-note strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .story-path ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .7rem 1.7rem; padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.3rem; }
  .story-path li { padding-left: .1rem; }
  .code-example { margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--structure); }
  .code-example figcaption { padding: .7rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: .8rem; }
  .code-example pre { padding: 1rem; margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; font-size: .85rem; }
  .test-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.8rem 0; }
  .test-pair > div { border-top: 1px solid var(--structure); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .test-pair h3 { margin: .5rem 0; }
  .return-path { display: flex; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.3rem 0; margin-top: 1.5rem; border-block: 2px solid var(--structure); }
  .return-path .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); }
  .return-path h3 { margin: .4rem 0; }
  .return-arrow { font-size: 2rem; color: var(--structure); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .test-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .story-path ol { display: grid; gap: .8rem; }
    .return-arrow { display: none; }
  }
</style>
